-  "One nonforking stdlib process, no network/subprocess/threads/signals/model/date helpers. Original monotonic deadline start+300s, checked inside callbacks, after every returned fixture write/close, after each case and throughout finalization, never renewed. No hard kernel-call preemption claim; only late returns are refused.",
-  "Exactly one JSON line per case (deferred included) plus final summary; bounded stdout and retained bytes. Exit0 only when every executable case MATCH, still NOT_QUALIFIED. Distinct nonzero codes:3 mismatch/error/ownership/protected-path change,4 declared inconclusive,5 deadline,6 byte budget,7 pre-case refusal. The process exit code is authoritative: an original-deadline crossing observed after the last case, after protected-state reads, during the provisional summary write, after final harness close or after the final summary emission returns yields exit5; a summary line emitted before a late return is then non-authoritative, and the on-disk summary remains PRE_FINAL_HARNESS_CLOSE_PROVISIONAL. Uninjected BaseException: compact emergency line and report retention are best effort, every secondary failure is latched by type and can never replace it; cleanup runs unconditionally under it; the original object propagates; caller keeps original reader/report.",
-  "Fault proxies load a separate namespace of the same verified reader and delegate real native operations. Native handles retained before post-call fault; exact dev/ino identities and original iterator objects retained; at most one owning close, no number-reuse inference. Instrumentation is labelled, never kernel provenance. Iterator count refers to explicit close; native iterator may internally close at EOF. Orphan cleanup runs as a finalizer that knows the in-flight exception: every withheld handle attempted once, every failure latched, an in-flight non-Exception BaseException never replaced.",
-  "Harness descriptor cleanup: exactly one close attempt per retained descriptor, never retried, every outcome latched (nonzero exit). A cleanup failure never replaces an in-flight non-Exception BaseException primary. With no primary or an ordinary-Exception primary, ordinary cleanup errors are latched and returned (an ordinary primary is preserved), while a newly arising non-Exception BaseException propagates after all attempts are retained.",
+  "One nonforking stdlib process, no network/subprocess/threads/signals/model/date helpers. Original monotonic deadline start+300s, checked inside callbacks, after every returned fixture write/close, after each case, after pre-case refusal cleanup and after its refusal summary, and after every finalization, fallback-emission and run-level-failure phase, never renewed; an unreadable clock counts as crossed. No hard kernel-call preemption claim; only late returns are refused.",
+  "Exactly one JSON line per case (deferred included) plus final summary while the output sink accepts them; bounded stdout (bytes reserved before each write, so a failed or partial write still counts) and bounded retained bytes. Exit0 only when every executable case MATCH, every record was delivered and no ownership latch is set, still NOT_QUALIFIED. Distinct nonzero codes with one fixed precedence: 5 deadline > 6 byte budget > 3 mismatch/error/ownership/protected-path change/undelivered record > 4 declared inconclusive; 7 pre-case refusal unless the original deadline is observed crossed (5). The process exit code is authoritative: deadline, budget and ordinary failures of case emission, fallback emission, protected-state reads, provisional summary persistence, final harness close, final summary emission or any other post-bootstrap step are classified after the required cleanup and never escape as an uncaught ordinary exception; an unavailable output sink can lose records, never the nonzero classification; an original-deadline crossing observed after the last case, after protected-state reads, during the provisional summary write, after final harness close or after the final summary emission returns yields exit5; a summary line emitted before a late return is then non-authoritative, and the on-disk summary remains PRE_FINAL_HARNESS_CLOSE_PROVISIONAL. Uninjected BaseException: compact emergency line, reader retention in one preallocated slot and report retention are best effort, each individually protected; every secondary or bookkeeping failure is latched (allocation-free flag first, bounded type list second) and can never replace it; cleanup runs unconditionally under it; the original object propagates; caller keeps original reader/report.",
+  "Fault proxies load a separate namespace of the same verified reader and delegate real native operations. Native handles retained before post-call fault; exact dev/ino identities and original iterator objects retained; at most one owning close, no number-reuse inference. Instrumentation is labelled, never kernel provenance. Iterator count refers to explicit close; native iterator may internally close at EOF. Every proxy violation is an allocation-free flag (no diagnostic list). Orphan cleanup runs as a finalizer that knows the in-flight exception: every withheld handle attempted once after its identity check, every outcome latched by the flag and kept on its record before anything else, an in-flight non-Exception BaseException never replaced.",
+  "Harness descriptor cleanup: exactly one close attempt per retained descriptor, never retried or double-closed. A failed attempt first sets the allocation-free ownership-uncertainty latch and keeps the actual exception on its row; only then is a bounded best-effort diagnostic copied (at most 16 rows of at most 200 characters), and a failure of that copy is itself latched and kept as an event. Exit refusal reads the latch, never diagnostic-list growth. Frozen R5 priority, not the PRT newest-origin rule: an active non-Exception BaseException primary is never replaced by any cleanup, diagnostic or bookkeeping failure; with no primary or an ordinary-Exception primary, the FIRST eligible newly arising non-Exception BaseException (close outcome, then its diagnostic, then sweep bookkeeping, in arising order) propagates only after every remaining row has had its single attempt; ordinary cleanup errors are latched and returned (an ordinary primary is preserved; without any primary a failed direct close fails its own operation). A sweep whose iteration faults resumes once, skipping attempted rows.",
+  "Interpreter failure boundary: harness bookkeeping, diagnostic formatting, list growth, report, retention and emission statements on cleanup, emergency, fallback and finalization paths are individually protected as above and diagnostic retention is bounded. Python frame, iterator, exception and traceback allocation inside the interpreter itself, and asynchronous exceptions delivered between protected statements, are outside the source guarantee: under allocation failure the interpreter itself can replace an in-flight exception, and a sweep whose iteration faults twice leaves its remaining rows unattempted with the uncertainty latch set (nonzero exit). No unbounded-allocation or OOM-completion guarantee is claimed.",
